From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] gxp/gs201: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx)

Port private/google-modules/gxp/gs201 to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - MODULE_IMPORT_NS() takes a string literal (6.13)

Files: gcip-kernel-driver/drivers/gcip/gcip-iommu.c, gxp-dmabuf.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.
---
diff --git a/gcip-kernel-driver/drivers/gcip/gcip-iommu.c b/gcip-kernel-driver/drivers/gcip/gcip-iommu.c
index 7b57441..41b4a17 100644
--- a/gcip-kernel-driver/drivers/gcip/gcip-iommu.c
+++ b/gcip-kernel-driver/drivers/gcip/gcip-iommu.c
@@ -1331,4 +1331,4 @@ void gcip_iommu_unmap(struct gcip_iommu_domain *domain, dma_addr_t iova, size_t
 			 size, unmapped);
 }
 
-MODULE_IMPORT_NS(DMA_BUF);
+MODULE_IMPORT_NS("DMA_BUF");
diff --git a/gxp-dmabuf.c b/gxp-dmabuf.c
index b88c696..6759871 100644
--- a/gxp-dmabuf.c
+++ b/gxp-dmabuf.c
@@ -89,4 +89,4 @@ err_dma_buf_put:
 	return ERR_PTR(ret);
 }
 
-MODULE_IMPORT_NS(DMA_BUF);
+MODULE_IMPORT_NS("DMA_BUF");
